Anisotropy, nonlinearity, locality and history (@em-constitutive: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1", #source "../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91", #electromagnetism "../currents/Drift-diffusion-relaxation-and-Ohm-law.lingua#r_3P3417NJ3B753K217S24RZY08D") { r_56YXQANA62QHAYXPAFSK9V43KQ
**Read:** [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1), matter and response assumptions; [Measuring Permittivity and Permeability — NIST TN 1536](../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91), constitutive definitions and material-measurement scope.

A constitutive relation connects field variables to a material state and a scale of description. In an anisotropic linear dielectric, D_i = Σ ε_ij E_j, so D and E need not be parallel. A reciprocal lossless electrostatic tensor has symmetry/positivity properties supporting a meaningful energy. Rotate the tensor with the coordinate system and test the result on the same physical field.

Ferroelectric hysteresis, field-dependent permittivity, saturation and spatial dispersion go beyond a fixed scalar constant. A graph of D versus E can depend on temperature, frequency, amplitude, preparation and the time path. Distinguish reversible stored energy from dissipation over a cycle and identify when an equilibrium constitutive function exists.

Build a material description specifying state, tensor or scalar form, linear range, frequency range and uncertainty. A dielectric constant quoted without frequency can conceal conduction or relaxation. A macroscopic local model may fail near interfaces or at short wavelengths. [General chemistry](../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V) and [Resources and materials — feedstocks, useful properties, production, and recovery](../../../../ergon/materials/Materials.lingua#r_14HP6K610XB12E2WGNK9A6VN8D) connect chemical composition and microstructure to these properties; microscopic/quantum explanations deepen rather than replace the boundary and conservation laws developed here.

